                    {
                        "translation_id": "672712e6-3bc8-49a1-bede-2b776cea2e1d",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab6434c3-c61f-3eb5-902f-15c433bcbaaa",
                        "source_sense_id": "d6b77dd1-985f-38b5-ad13-e43afbe5aac9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Calvinistic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Calvinistic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e20644a-50ee-3f68-8055-3009537a8a61",
                                        "entry_id": "21e6d0d8-5139-38f8-a551-b5151fcee00d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of Calvinist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14c18e3d-9d9e-4c31-b7c3-0a3d50d105ae",
                                                "sense_id": "4e20644a-50ee-3f68-8055-3009537a8a61",
                                                "text": "Their Captain's announcement was listened to by the throng of standing sailors in a dumbness like that of a seated congregation of believers in hell listening to the clergyman's announcement of his Calvinistic text."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8ba2c719-6e6e-4e31-925d-a8711ad674b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab6434c3-c61f-3eb5-902f-15c433bcbaaa",
                        "source_sense_id": "d6b77dd1-985f-38b5-ad13-e43afbe5aac9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Calvinistical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Calvinistical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27b422a6-e116-3891-9b6f-61c57353d9d9",
                                        "entry_id": "0e1f877f-14cb-3572-b01a-4a846b312917",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of Calvinist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76c8bd46-1b82-4df1-9151-62fc73e46410",
                                                "sense_id": "27b422a6-e116-3891-9b6f-61c57353d9d9",
                                                "text": "1774, Dr Samuel Johnson, Preface to the Works of the English Poets, J. Nichols, Volume II, Page 138,\n\"His theological opinions are said to have been first calvinistical;...\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9606b0d9-6bbf-48f1-9ce9-8cdd0abe6537",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab6434c3-c61f-3eb5-902f-15c433bcbaaa",
                        "source_sense_id": "d6b77dd1-985f-38b5-ad13-e43afbe5aac9",
                        "target_lang_word": "calvinista",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "calvinista",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d84fd2bc-3dcc-3c74-961b-cdcf4e2a740c",
                                        "entry_id": "645a54ba-0536-3a0a-98fb-a80d2096c5f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Que pertenece o concierne al religioso protestante Juan Calvino o el calvinismo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "noun"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3189d343-b42c-4e6e-9ea3-fd19af8e8347",
                                                "sense_id": "d84fd2bc-3dcc-3c74-961b-cdcf4e2a740c",
                                                "text": "¡Si de Sión con la real conquista\nHiciese á mi gran rey sacro diadema\nLa santa paz del Cristianismo, vista\nEn un divino presupuesto y tema,\nDespues que á la. insolencia calvinista,\nHerética, cismática y blasfema,\nSu primer golpe echase en el profundo\nMar de su error sacrílego y inmundo!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86ec11da-42c4-47fc-b076-6c0fe7457121",
                                                "sense_id": "d84fd2bc-3dcc-3c74-961b-cdcf4e2a740c",
                                                "text": "entre el ‘mysterium tremendum’ de la tradición judía y la omnipotencia hasta el arbitrio de la imagen calvinista, Hooker especula una noción de Dios como principio absoluto del orden del Universo."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb510d40-2d74-3f0c-9f7d-8577df2ef17e",
                                        "entry_id": "645a54ba-0536-3a0a-98fb-a80d2096c5f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Seguidor del calvinismo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "noun"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bd72446-c358-44ae-b7ed-8a7e191bb304",
                                                "sense_id": "eb510d40-2d74-3f0c-9f7d-8577df2ef17e",
                                                "text": "Haced en Ingalaterra\nnobilísimo cerote,\nreduciendo al calvinista,\nsaqueando al hugonote!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "037b1fb6-3544-4721-9451-3f9e18405d94",
                                                "sense_id": "eb510d40-2d74-3f0c-9f7d-8577df2ef17e",
                                                "text": "Carecían de fe, pero en su sangre perduraban, como rastros oscuros, el duro fanatismo del calvinista y las supersticiones del pampa."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
